1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,680
(Priya:)Does that sound like fun?
Yeah!

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:05,480
(Leonard:)Dodgers are baseball,
right?

3
00:00:05,490 --> 00:00:07,550
(Priya:)You'll need to explain
the game to me.

4
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:08,990
(Leonard:)Mm, it's complicated.

5
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:11,060
(Leonard:)But as I remember it,
the essentials are

6
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:14,390
"get chosen last, get hit
by the ball, cry, go home."

7
00:00:14,390 --> 00:00:18,030
(Priya:)Well, regardless,
I've got four tickets.

8
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:20,530
(Priya:)And I was thinking we can bring
Bernadette and Howard.

9
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:24,000
(Priya:)She's really interesting,
and I bet I can get used to him.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,900
(Leonard:)Well, it might not
be a great idea

11
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:28,340
(Leonard:)to invite those two.
Why not?

12
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:30,170
(Leonard:)Don't tell anybody
I told you,

13
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:32,180
(Leonard:)but I heard she might
be breaking up with him.

14
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:34,050
(Priya:)Oh... too bad...

15
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:36,430
(Priya:)Although I do know one person
for whom that's good news.

16
00:00:36,430 --> 00:00:37,580
(Leonard:)Really? Who?

17
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:38,850
(Priya:)My brother.

18
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:40,220
(Priya:)He's got a big crush
on Bernadette.

19
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,560
(Sheldon:)What?

20
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:46,660
(Priya:)You're kidding.

21
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:49,610
No. I found poems
he wrote about her.

22
00:00:49,610 --> 00:00:51,030
(Priya:)Very disturbing.

23
00:00:51,030 --> 00:00:55,230
"Oh, Bernadette,
please play my clarinet."

24
00:00:57,040 --> 00:01:00,440
(Leonard:)Wow, that's hard to believe.
Yes.

